# application.blacklist — values that MUST NOT fill the {application} slot
# (OVOS-INTENT-2 §4.3 slot-value exclusion).
#
# The {application} slot is open-vocabulary and the verbs "open"/"close" are
# shared with many other skills, so without this list "open {application}" and
# "close {application}" would swallow utterances that are not about desktop
# applications at all. Each entry names a phrase that is never an application;
# when it is the candidate slot value the match is dropped so the intent
# pipeline can route the utterance to its rightful skill. The concrete
# conflicting utterance is cited beside each group.

# Anaphoric pronouns / deictics — refer back to something, never name an app.
# "open it", "close that", "open this one"
isso
isto
aquilo
eles
estes
aqueles

# Home-automation openables — owned by Home Assistant / PHAL skills.
# "open the garage door", "close the blinds", "open the gate"
[a] porta
[as] portas
[a porta d]a garagem
[o] portão
[os] estores
[as] cortinas
[as] persianas

# Content skills.
# "open the news"    -> ovos-skill-news
# "open the camera"  -> camera skill
# "open the weather" -> weather skill
[as] notícias
[a] câmara
[o] tempo

# System / power skills.
# "shut down the computer", "close the system"
[o] computador
[o] sistema
[o] pc
